 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Which computer is faster? The answer depends on what you measure, and exams love the cases where the obvious answer is wrong."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Performance metrics"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "What time means, the CPU time equation, and the CPI of a mix of instructions."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the two classic traps: a faster clock that loses, and fewer instructions or more MIPS that lose."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[3..=4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then how to average over several programs, and one exam question that uses everything."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[5..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "time",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: there are two different things people mean by time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: what we measure"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "defs"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Response time, or elapsed time, is the wall-clock time from start to finish. It includes disk, input and output, and time spent waiting for other programs."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "defs[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "CPU time counts only the time the processor spends on this task: user time plus system time, with no waiting."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "defs[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Throughput is how many tasks finish per unit time, for example jobs per hour on a server."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "defs[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The two can move separately. A faster processor improves both response time and throughput."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "defs"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "upg"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "upg[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "But adding processors, with one task each, leaves every task just as slow, while more tasks finish per hour: better throughput, same response time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "upg[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now, how do we say one machine is faster? Performance is one over execution time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "upg"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "fast"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fast[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "X is n times faster than Y when n equals Y's time divided by X's time. The slower machine's time goes on top."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "fast[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fast[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If A takes 10 seconds and B takes 15, A is 15 over 10, that is 1.5 times faster."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "fast[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fast[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: A is 50 percent faster, but it takes only 33 percent less time. Those are different numbers, so read which one the question asks for."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "fast[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fast[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "n = time of slower ÷ time of faster · \"% faster\" ≠ \"% less time\""
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "equation",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the one equation behind every numerical question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: the CPU time equation"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "fast"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "eq"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "CPU time equals instruction count, times cycles per instruction, times the clock cycle time. Or, divide by the clock rate instead of multiplying by the cycle time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "eq[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Check the units: instructions per program, times cycles per instruction, times seconds per cycle, gives seconds per program."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "eq[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "eq[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: questions give the clock rate in gigahertz. A 2 gigahertz clock has a cycle time of one over 2 times 10 to the 9, which is 0.5 nanoseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "eq[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "eq[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So 2 billion instructions at CPI 1.5 on that clock take 1.5 seconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "eq[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "eq[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Which design choices change which factor? The algorithm and the compiler change both the instruction count and the CPI."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "eq"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "who"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "who[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The instruction set can change all three. The hardware organization changes CPI and the clock, and chip technology changes only the clock."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "who[2..=4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "No single factor tells you the speed. Only the product of all three does."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "CPU time = IC × CPI × cycle time = IC × CPI ÷ f"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mix",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: real programs mix instructions with different CPIs, so the CPI we use is a weighted average."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: CPI of a mix"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "who"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "mix"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Multiply each class's share by its CPI. ALU: 0.45 times 1 is 0.45."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mix[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mix[0][3]",
       "value": "0.45",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Loads: 0.25 times 2 is 0.5. Stores: 0.1 times 2 is 0.2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mix[1..=2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mix[1][3]",
       "value": "0.50",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mix[2][3]",
       "value": "0.20",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Branches: 0.2 times 3 is 0.6."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mix[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mix[3][3]",
       "value": "0.60",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Add them: the average CPI is 1.75."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mix[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mix[4][3]",
       "value": "CPI = 1.75",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: if the question gives instruction counts instead of percentages, add up the cycles and divide by the total number of instructions. Never just average the CPI column."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mix.CPI"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case two: a machine that issues several instructions per cycle can have a CPI below 1. Then we often quote IPC, instructions per cycle, which is one over CPI."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "CPI = Σ (share × CPI of class) · IPC = 1 ÷ CPI"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "clock",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4, the first trap: same program, same instruction set. A runs at 2 gigahertz with CPI 2. B runs at 3 gigahertz with CPI 3.2. Which is faster?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: a faster clock can lose"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "mix"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "clk"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The instruction count is the same, so compare time per instruction: CPI times cycle time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "clk[0][3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "clk[1][3]",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A: 2 cycles of 0.5 nanoseconds is 1 nanosecond per instruction."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "clk[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "clk[0][3]",
       "value": "2 × 0.5 ns = 1.0 ns",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "B: 3.2 cycles of a third of a nanosecond is about 1.067 nanoseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "clk[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "clk[1][3]",
       "value": "3.2 ÷ 3 ns ≈ 1.067 ns",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So A, with the slower clock, is about 1.067 times faster. A higher clock rate alone proves nothing."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "clk[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "compare IC × CPI ÷ f, never the clock alone"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The same equation answers design questions. A program takes 10 seconds on a 2 gigahertz machine, so it needs 20 billion cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "clk"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "need"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "need[0]"
      }
     ]
